   - Time = distance / rate = 45 miles / 30 mph = 1.5 hours

3. **Calculate the distance from City \( A \) where they will meet.** 
   - Alicia bikes at 18 miles per hour, so in 1.5 hours, she will have biked \( 18 \text{ mph} \times 1.5 \text{ hours} \).

