Let \theta denote the acute angle formed by lines $l_{1}$ and $l_{2}$. \tan\theta={3\over2}
To find the acute angle $\theta$, we use the formula for the tangent of the angle between two lines: $\tan\theta = \left|\frac{m_2 - m_1}{1 + m_1m_2}\right|$. Here, $m_1 = 2$ and $m_2 = \frac{1}{3}$. Thus, $\tan\theta = \left|\frac{\frac{1}{3} - 2}{1 + 2 \cdot \frac{1}{3}}\right| = \left|\frac{-\frac{5}{3}}{\frac{5}{3}}\right| = \left|-1\right| = 1$. Therefore, $\theta = \arctan(1) = 45^{\circ}$.
